Falsifies `system_tests::user::terminal_display_swap_tests::the_display_terminal_is_replaced_live_and_its_screen_and_history_survive`.

Architecture: aarch64

The patch makes an absorbing `display_terminal` drop its scrollback's length, so the replacement
keeps the screen and loses the history. Every pixel still matches, because the live view never
shows history; the comparison of the blob carried home is what catches it, which is the reason the
test reads the reserve at all.

Expected to fail: "the first swap: the blob carried home differs from the engine's at byte 24" in
the blob comparison, after the screen comparison has passed. Replayed red at exactly that assertion
on aarch64 on 2026-10-19 (UTC).

